// Fixture (not a standalone test): the IMPORTED half of the imported-module
// diagnostic-location oracle. Compiled on its own it is expected to be rejected --
// the E3030 below is deliberate. bin/t_diagloc_mod.ax imports it, and the harness
// block asserts that the diagnostic names THIS file and the line the `let` is on
// (currently 12 — if you add or remove a line above it, update the harness block too),
// proving an imported
// module's tree carries a source map. Before that fix it printed only
// "at byte offset N of the compilation unit".
//
// Since B5 (an imported module's own diagnostics halt the importing build), the IMPORTER
// bin/t_diagloc_mod.ax is rejected too, where it used to produce an executable. The
// harness block is unaffected — it asserts on the rendered diagnostic, not on an exe.
pub fn helper() -> i64:
    let bad: u8 = 300
    return bad as i64
